  <teiHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>A Study of Photosynthesis in Controlled Environments</title>
      </titleStmt>
    </fileDesc>
  </teiHeader>
  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>1 Introduction</head>
        <pb n="1"/>
        <p>Photosynthesis is the process by which plants convert light energy into
        chemical energy. This paper investigates the rate of photosynthesis under
        controlled greenhouse conditions.</p>
        <div>
          <head>1.1 Background</head>
          <p>Prior work has established the basic biochemistry of the Calvin cycle,
          but few studies control for humidity and CO2 concentration simultaneously.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>2 Methods</head>
        <pb n="2"/>
        <p>We used a randomized controlled trial design with three greenhouse
        chambers, each held at a different CO2 concentration.</p>
        <div>
          <head>2.1 Data collection</head>
          <p>Leaf samples were collected every six hours over a two week period
          and analyzed with a gas exchange analyzer.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </body>
